<?xml version="1.0" ?>
<!--
  warehouse_ver2.sdf . m5_ver2 Step 5's OWN warehouse, an open relayout of
  sim/worlds/warehouse.sdf. That file is not modified and keeps the dense
  M4/M5 layout (m5_ver2/CLAUDE.md: the existing tree is used where it is,
  unmodified); this copy will drift from it, and that is intended, exactly
  as m5_ver2's forklift_ver2/model.sdf drifts from agv/forklift/model.sdf.

  WHY THIS COPY EXISTS. Owner instruction, 2026-08-12: the source world's
  aisles are tight enough that driving trips the protective field at once.
  m5_ver2/step5/ipc/field_eval.py evaluates, per monitoring case,
  PF/WF = 1.0/2.5 (case 1), 2.2/3.7 (case 2), 4.5/6.0 (case 3) metres, and
  the vehicle's plan envelope is 1.04 m wide, so a 3.80 m aisle leaves
  1.38 m of lateral clearance - inside case 2's protective field with the
  vehicle perfectly centred. The paths here are sized against those
  numbers, not against taste.

  WHAT CHANGED, AND NOTHING ELSE DID:
    . RackRowC (both runs), BuildingColumns and TransferStationFrame are
      DELETED. Grep for any of them must return nothing.
    . Rack runs are 3 bays (4 frames), not 4 bays (5 frames).
    . Row B moved south, widening the one drive aisle between the rows.
    . The hall shell (30.0 x 20.0, walls at x = +-15.00, y = +-10.00),
      physics, plugins, the GUI block, Floor, walls, DoorGap,
      ConveyorStation, both charge bays and every painted marking are the
      source world's, byte for byte, except the GUI comment's topic-list
      note (this vehicle's sorted entry zero is the BACK scanner).
      The world name stays "warehouse": every topic, launch and script
      keys on it.

     +y
      ^   north wall, inner face y = +10.00
      |  ##############  RackRowA  (single deep)   y in [8.90, 10.00]
      |  ===== MAIN AISLE, centreline y = +5.65, 6.50 m clear =====
      |  ##############  RackRowB  (back to back)  y in [-0.10, 2.40]
      |
      |  ========= OPEN SOUTH BLOCK, y in [-10.00, -0.10] =========
      |  9.90 m deep: dock apron, spawn, safety zone, both charge bays
      |  [ChargeBay1] [ChargeBay2]        [DoorGap x in [4.00, 8.00]]
      +======================================================> +x
         west end aisle       central cross aisle      east end aisle
         x in [-15.0, -10.0]  x in [-3.10, +3.10]      x in [10.0, 15.0]
         5.00 m               6.20 m                   5.00 m

  CLEARANCES, CENTRED, SCANNER TO NEAREST FACE (envelope half width
  0.52 m): main aisle 2.73 m - clear of case 2 PF (2.2) and case 1 WF
  (2.5); cross aisle 2.58 m - the same; end aisles 1.98 m - clear of
  case 1 PF with double margin, inside case 2 PF, so a mid-speed pass
  down an end aisle is expected to demand a stop and that is the field
  doing its job, not a defect. The east end aisle narrows to 4.00 m
  beside the ConveyorStation deck. Case 3 (4.5/6.0) is the fallback for
  an unreadable monitoring case and is satisfied nowhere indoors except
  the middle of the south block; that is unchanged from the source world
  and is a property of any 20 m hall.

  ==================== RACK GEOMETRY, BY RULE ====================

    upright section        0.10 (x) by 0.08 (y), 4.00 high
    bay pitch              2.30 m, so a 6.90 m run is 4 frames and 3 bays
    frame x, west run      -10.00, -7.70, -5.40, -3.10
    frame x, east run       +3.10, +5.40, +7.70, +10.00
    bay centre x           midway between adjacent frames
    sub row depth          1.10 m, uprights 0.04 m inside each face
    back to back flue      0.30 m between the two sub rows of row B
    stock unit             2.10 (x) by 1.00 (y), set 0.05 m back from the
                           aisle face, so the uprights stand proud of it
    floor level stock      z in [0.00, 1.40], present in EVERY bay
    reserve level stock    z in [1.50, 2.70]: east runs all three bays
                           loaded, west runs bays 0 and 2 only - the same
                           goods-in-east, picked-west rule the source
                           world states and WAREHOUSE_LANDMARKS.md
                           measured.

  Row A sub row: faces y = 8.90/10.00, uprights 8.940/9.960, stock 9.450.
  Row B north:   faces y = 2.40/1.30,  uprights 2.360/1.340,  stock 1.850.
  Row B south:   faces y = -0.10/1.00, uprights -0.060/0.940, stock 0.450.

  The physics step is the source world's 2 ms at 500 Hz; the GUI block is
  the source world's, so the beams stay three clicks in (refresh, then
  topic). The spawn this step uses, (-3.00, -5.50), sits in the open
  south block with 4.50 m to the south wall and 5.40 m to row B.
-->
<sdf version="1.8">
  <world name="warehouse">

    <!-- The arena's 2 ms fixed step at 500 Hz, so joint rates measured on
         the M4 arena stay comparable here. -->
    <physics type="ode">
      <max_step_size>0.002</max_step_size>
      <real_time_factor>1.0</real_time_factor>
      <real_time_update_rate>500</real_time_update_rate>
    </physics>

    <plugin name="gz::sim::systems::Physics" filename="libgz-sim-physics-system.so"/>
    <plugin name="gz::sim::systems::UserCommands" filename="libgz-sim-user-commands-system.so"/>
    <plugin name="gz::sim::systems::SceneBroadcaster" filename="libgz-sim-scene-broadcaster-system.so"/>

    <!-- Required by the vehicle's three gpu_lidar sensors. Without this no
         scan topic is ever advertised and the failure is silent. -->
    <plugin name="gz::sim::systems::Sensors" filename="libgz-sim-sensors-system.so">
      <render_engine>ogre2</render_engine>
    </plugin>

    <!-- ======================= GUI CONFIGURATION ====================== -->
    <!--
      THIS BLOCK IS WHY THE LIDAR BEAMS ARE VISIBLE, and it is the arena's
      block with the camera moved. worlds/forklift_arena.sdf carries the
      full measured rationale for every plugin here and is the file to read
      and to edit; it is not repeated line for line because two copies of a
      long explanation drift apart. The three facts a viewer of THIS world
      needs are repeated, because getting them wrong is silent:

        1. `<visualize>true</visualize>` on a sensor is NECESSARY BUT NOT
           SUFFICIENT on Gazebo Harmonic. VisualizeLidar is what draws laser
           scans, it is not in gz sim's default GUI configuration, and it
           never reads the sensor's visualize flag. Loading it is this
           block's whole job.
        2. Nothing is drawn until a human presses the plugin's refresh
           button. Beams on is not the start state of this world.
        3. Refresh selects entry ZERO of a sorted topic list, which is
           /forklift/gz/safety_scanner_back/measurement, NOT the navigation
           lidar. Those beams are a non safe measurement channel and are not
           a protective field (invariant 1). A recording that leaves the
           default selection is showing the wrong sensor with the most
           dangerous available caption. The navigation lidar is
           /forklift/gz/scan_nav.

      The scene settings below are repeated from the world's <scene> element
      on purpose: MinimalScene does not inherit them.
    -->
    <gui fullscreen="0">

      <plugin filename="MinimalScene" name="3D View">
        <gz-gui>
          <title>3D View</title>
          <property type="bool" key="showTitleBar">false</property>
          <property type="string" key="state">docked</property>
        </gz-gui>
        <engine>ogre2</engine>
        <scene>scene</scene>
        <ambient_light>1.0 1.0 1.0</ambient_light>
        <background_color>0.7 0.7 0.7</background_color>
        <!-- Looking north east from over the south west corner, so the
             dock apron, both charging bays and the west end of the rack
             block are in frame with no camera move. -->
        <camera_pose>-19.0 -16.0 12.0 0 0.52 0.72</camera_pose>
      </plugin>

      <plugin filename="GzSceneManager" name="Scene Manager">
        <gz-gui>
          <property key="resizable" type="bool">false</property>
          <property key="width" type="double">5</property>
          <property key="height" type="double">5</property>
          <property key="state" type="string">floating</property>
          <property key="showTitleBar" type="bool">false</property>
        </gz-gui>
      </plugin>

      <plugin filename="InteractiveViewControl" name="Interactive view control">
        <gz-gui>
          <property key="resizable" type="bool">false</property>
          <property key="width" type="double">5</property>
          <property key="height" type="double">5</property>
          <property key="state" type="string">floating</property>
          <property key="showTitleBar" type="bool">false</property>
        </gz-gui>
      </plugin>

      <plugin filename="CameraTracking" name="Camera Tracking">
        <gz-gui>
          <property key="resizable" type="bool">false</property>
          <property key="width" type="double">5</property>
          <property key="height" type="double">5</property>
          <property key="state" type="string">floating</property>
          <property key="showTitleBar" type="bool">false</property>
        </gz-gui>
      </plugin>

      <plugin filename="EntityContextMenuPlugin" name="Entity context menu">
        <gz-gui>
          <property key="state" type="string">floating</property>
          <property key="width" type="double">5</property>
          <property key="height" type="double">5</property>
          <property key="showTitleBar" type="bool">false</property>
        </gz-gui>
      </plugin>

      <!-- NOT start_paused. The scanners are always_on but the sensors
           system renders on simulation steps, so a paused world publishes
           no scan, the plugin's topic list comes up empty and the beams
           never appear. The world is launched with -r for the same
           reason. -->
      <plugin filename="WorldControl" name="World control">
        <gz-gui>
          <title>World control</title>
          <property type="bool" key="showTitleBar">false</property>
          <property type="bool" key="resizable">false</property>
          <property type="double" key="height">72</property>
          <property type="double" key="z">1</property>
          <property type="string" key="state">floating</property>
          <anchors target="3D View">
            <line own="left" target="left"/>
            <line own="bottom" target="bottom"/>
          </anchors>
        </gz-gui>
        <play_pause>true</play_pause>
        <step>true</step>
        <start_paused>false</start_paused>
        <use_event>true</use_event>
      </plugin>

      <!-- The real time factor readout, on screen for any recording. It is
           NOT a measurement instrument: the value it shows is gz's smoothed
           instantaneous factor. -->
      <plugin filename="WorldStats" name="World stats">
        <gz-gui>
          <title>World stats</title>
          <property type="bool" key="showTitleBar">false</property>
          <property type="bool" key="resizable">false</property>
          <property type="double" key="height">110</property>
          <property type="double" key="width">290</property>
          <property type="double" key="z">1</property>
          <property type="string" key="state">floating</property>
          <anchors target="3D View">
            <line own="right" target="right"/>
            <line own="bottom" target="bottom"/>
          </anchors>
        </gz-gui>
        <sim_time>true</sim_time>
        <real_time>true</real_time>
        <real_time_factor>true</real_time_factor>
        <iterations>true</iterations>
      </plugin>

      <!-- The beams. Docked rather than floating so the topic and display
           type combo boxes are visible without hunting: which scanner is on
           screen is not guessable from the picture. -->
      <plugin filename="VisualizeLidar" name="Visualize Lidar">
        <gz-gui>
          <title>Visualize lidar</title>
          <property type="string" key="state">docked</property>
        </gz-gui>
      </plugin>

      <plugin filename="Screenshot" name="Screenshot">
        <gz-gui>
          <property type="bool" key="showTitleBar">false</property>
          <property type="string" key="state">floating</property>
          <property type="double" key="width">100</property>
          <property type="double" key="height">50</property>
        </gz-gui>
      </plugin>

    </gui>

    <scene>
      <ambient>1 1 1 1</ambient>
      <background>0.7 0.7 0.7 1</background>
      <shadows>false</shadows>
      <grid>false</grid>
    </scene>

    <light name="sun" type="directional">
      <cast_shadows>false</cast_shadows>
      <pose>0 0 12 0 0 0</pose>
      <diffuse>1.0 1.0 1.0 1</diffuse>
      <specular>0.2 0.2 0.2 1</specular>
      <direction>-0.3 0.3 -1.0</direction>
    </light>

    <gravity>0 0 -9.8</gravity>

    <!-- ============================ Floor ============================ -->
    <!-- Plain concrete, mu 1.0 as in the arena: the tricycle has a single
         driven wheel and a slippery floor turns traction figures into tyre
         slip figures. -->
    <model name="Floor">
      <static>true</static>
      <link name="link">
        <collision name="collision">
          <geometry>
            <plane><normal>0 0 1</normal><size>30 20</size></plane>
          </geometry>
          <surface>
            <friction><ode><mu>1.0</mu><mu2>1.0</mu2></ode></friction>
          </surface>
        </collision>
        <visual name="visual">
          <geometry>
            <plane><normal>0 0 1</normal><size>30 20</size></plane>
          </geometry>
          <material>
            <ambient>0.55 0.55 0.55 1</ambient>
            <diffuse>0.55 0.55 0.55 1</diffuse>
          </material>
        </visual>
      </link>
    </model>

    <!-- ======================= Perimeter walls ======================= -->
    <!-- 0.20 thick, 4.00 high, inner faces at x = +-15.00 and
         y = +-10.00. The south wall is in two segments leaving the
         4.00 m dock door opening at x in [4.00, 8.00]. -->
    <model name="WallNorth">
      <static>true</static>
      <link name="link">
        <collision name="wallnorth_collision">
          <pose>0.000 10.100 2.000 0 0 0</pose>
          <geometry><box><size>30.600 0.200 4.000</size></box></geometry>
        </collision>
        <visual name="wallnorth_visual">
          <pose>0.000 10.100 2.000 0 0 0</pose>
          <geometry><box><size>30.600 0.200 4.000</size></box></geometry>
          <material><ambient>0.80 0.80 0.75 1</ambient><diffuse>0.80 0.80 0.75 1</diffuse></material>
        </visual>
      </link>
    </model>

    <model name="WallSouthWest">
      <static>true</static>
      <link name="link">
        <collision name="wallsouthwest_collision">
          <pose>-5.600 -10.100 2.000 0 0 0</pose>
          <geometry><box><size>19.200 0.200 4.000</size></box></geometry>
        </collision>
        <visual name="wallsouthwest_visual">
          <pose>-5.600 -10.100 2.000 0 0 0</pose>
          <geometry><box><size>19.200 0.200 4.000</size></box></geometry>
          <material><ambient>0.80 0.80 0.75 1</ambient><diffuse>0.80 0.80 0.75 1</diffuse></material>
        </visual>
      </link>
    </model>

    <model name="WallSouthEast">
      <static>true</static>
      <link name="link">
        <collision name="wallsoutheast_collision">
          <pose>11.600 -10.100 2.000 0 0 0</pose>
          <geometry><box><size>7.200 0.200 4.000</size></box></geometry>
        </collision>
        <visual name="wallsoutheast_visual">
          <pose>11.600 -10.100 2.000 0 0 0</pose>
          <geometry><box><size>7.200 0.200 4.000</size></box></geometry>
          <material><ambient>0.80 0.80 0.75 1</ambient><diffuse>0.80 0.80 0.75 1</diffuse></material>
        </visual>
      </link>
    </model>

    <model name="WallEast">
      <static>true</static>
      <link name="link">
        <collision name="walleast_collision">
          <pose>15.100 0.000 2.000 0 0 0</pose>
          <geometry><box><size>0.200 20.000 4.000</size></box></geometry>
        </collision>
        <visual name="walleast_visual">
          <pose>15.100 0.000 2.000 0 0 0</pose>
          <geometry><box><size>0.200 20.000 4.000</size></box></geometry>
          <material><ambient>0.80 0.80 0.75 1</ambient><diffuse>0.80 0.80 0.75 1</diffuse></material>
        </visual>
      </link>
    </model>

    <model name="WallWest">
      <static>true</static>
      <link name="link">
        <collision name="wallwest_collision">
          <pose>-15.100 0.000 2.000 0 0 0</pose>
          <geometry><box><size>0.200 20.000 4.000</size></box></geometry>
        </collision>
        <visual name="wallwest_visual">
          <pose>-15.100 0.000 2.000 0 0 0</pose>
          <geometry><box><size>0.200 20.000 4.000</size></box></geometry>
          <material><ambient>0.80 0.80 0.75 1</ambient><diffuse>0.80 0.80 0.75 1</diffuse></material>
        </visual>
      </link>
    </model>

    <!-- ========================= Dock door frame ====================== -->
    <!-- Two posts and a lintel marking the 4.00 m opening in the south
         wall. The opening itself stays free so the vehicle can drive
         through; the PLC controlled door acts here at M6 (ADR 0010). The
         posts cross both scan planes, the lintel crosses neither. -->
    <model name="DoorGap">
      <static>true</static>
      <pose>6.00 -10.10 0 0 0 0</pose>
      <link name="link">
        <collision name="post_west_collision">
          <pose>-2.100 0.000 1.750 0 0 0</pose>
          <geometry><box><size>0.200 0.300 3.500</size></box></geometry>
        </collision>
        <visual name="post_west_visual">
          <pose>-2.100 0.000 1.750 0 0 0</pose>
          <geometry><box><size>0.200 0.300 3.500</size></box></geometry>
          <material><ambient>0.90 0.60 0.10 1</ambient><diffuse>0.90 0.60 0.10 1</diffuse></material>
        </visual>
        <collision name="post_east_collision">
          <pose>2.100 0.000 1.750 0 0 0</pose>
          <geometry><box><size>0.200 0.300 3.500</size></box></geometry>
        </collision>
        <visual name="post_east_visual">
          <pose>2.100 0.000 1.750 0 0 0</pose>
          <geometry><box><size>0.200 0.300 3.500</size></box></geometry>
          <material><ambient>0.90 0.60 0.10 1</ambient><diffuse>0.90 0.60 0.10 1</diffuse></material>
        </visual>
        <collision name="lintel_collision">
          <pose>0.000 0.000 3.650 0 0 0</pose>
          <geometry><box><size>4.400 0.300 0.300</size></box></geometry>
        </collision>
        <visual name="lintel_visual">
          <pose>0.000 0.000 3.650 0 0 0</pose>
          <geometry><box><size>4.400 0.300 0.300</size></box></geometry>
          <material><ambient>0.90 0.60 0.10 1</ambient><diffuse>0.90 0.60 0.10 1</diffuse></material>
        </visual>
      </link>
    </model>

    <!-- ============================ Racking =========================== -->
    <!-- Four models: two rows, each cut into a west and an east run by
         the central cross aisle. Every primitive follows the parametric
         rules in the file header. Row A is single deep against the north
         wall; row B is a back to back pair. Row C and the building
         columns of the source world are deliberately absent here. -->

    <model name="RackRowA_West">
      <static>true</static>
      <link name="link">
        <!-- sub row A, front face y = +8.90, rear face y = +10.00 -->
        <collision name="a_frame0_front_collision">
          <pose>-10.000 8.940 2.000 0 0 0</pose>
          <geometry><box><size>0.100 0.080 4.000</size></box></geometry>
        </collision>
        <visual name="a_frame0_front_visual">
          <pose>-10.000 8.940 2.000 0 0 0</pose>
          <geometry><box><size>0.100 0.080 4.000</size></box></geometry>
          <material><ambient>0.85 0.35 0.10 1</ambient><diffuse>0.85 0.35 0.10 1</diffuse></material>
        </visual>
        <collision name="a_frame0_rear_collision">
          <pose>-10.000 9.960 2.000 0 0 0</pose>
          <geometry><box><size>0.100 0.080 4.000</size></box></geometry>
        </collision>
        <visual name="a_frame0_rear_visual">
          <pose>-10.000 9.960 2.000 0 0 0</pose>
          <geometry><box><size>0.100 0.080 4.000</size></box></geometry>
          <material><ambient>0.85 0.35 0.10 1</ambient><diffuse>0.85 0.35 0.10 1</diffuse></material>
        </visual>
        <collision name="a_frame1_front_collision">
          <pose>-7.700 8.940 2.000 0 0 0</pose>
          <geometry><box><size>0.100 0.080 4.000</size></box></geometry>
        </collision>
        <visual name="a_frame1_front_visual">
          <pose>-7.700 8.940 2.000 0 0 0</pose>
          <geometry><box><size>0.100 0.080 4.000</size></box></geometry>
          <material><ambient>0.85 0.35 0.10 1</ambient><diffuse>0.85 0.35 0.10 1</diffuse></material>
        </visual>
        <collision name="a_frame1_rear_collision">
          <pose>-7.700 9.960 2.000 0 0 0</pose>
          <geometry><box><size>0.100 0.080 4.000</size></box></geometry>
        </collision>
        <visual name="a_frame1_rear_visual">
          <pose>-7.700 9.960 2.000 0 0 0</pose>
          <geometry><box><size>0.100 0.080 4.000</size></box></geometry>
          <material><ambient>0.85 0.35 0.10 1</ambient><diffuse>0.85 0.35 0.10 1</diffuse></material>
        </visual>
        <collision name="a_frame2_front_collision">
          <pose>-5.400 8.940 2.000 0 0 0</pose>
          <geometry><box><size>0.100 0.080 4.000</size></box></geometry>
        </collision>
        <visual name="a_frame2_front_visual">
          <pose>-5.400 8.940 2.000 0 0 0</pose>
          <geometry><box><size>0.100 0.080 4.000</size></box></geometry>
          <material><ambient>0.85 0.35 0.10 1</ambient><diffuse>0.85 0.35 0.10 1</diffuse></material>
        </visual>
        <collision name="a_frame2_rear_collision">
          <pose>-5.400 9.960 2.000 0 0 0</pose>
          <geometry><box><size>0.100 0.080 4.000</size></box></geometry>
        </collision>
        <visual name="a_frame2_rear_visual">
          <pose>-5.400 9.960 2.000 0 0 0</pose>
          <geometry><box><size>0.100 0.080 4.000</size></box></geometry>
          <material><ambient>0.85 0.35 0.10 1</ambient><diffuse>0.85 0.35 0.10 1</diffuse></material>
        </visual>
        <collision name="a_frame3_front_collision">
          <pose>-3.100 8.940 2.000 0 0 0</pose>
          <geometry><box><size>0.100 0.080 4.000</size></box></geometry>
        </collision>
        <visual name="a_frame3_front_visual">
          <pose>-3.100 8.940 2.000 0 0 0</pose>
          <geometry><box><size>0.100 0.080 4.000</size></box></geometry>
          <material><ambient>0.85 0.35 0.10 1</ambient><diffuse>0.85 0.35 0.10 1</diffuse></material>
        </visual>
        <collision name="a_frame3_rear_collision">
          <pose>-3.100 9.960 2.000 0 0 0</pose>
          <geometry><box><size>0.100 0.080 4.000</size></box></geometry>
        </collision>
        <visual name="a_frame3_rear_visual">
          <pose>-3.100 9.960 2.000 0 0 0</pose>
          <geometry><box><size>0.100 0.080 4.000</size></box></geometry>
          <material><ambient>0.85 0.35 0.10 1</ambient><diffuse>0.85 0.35 0.10 1</diffuse></material>
        </visual>
        <collision name="a_bay0_level1_collision">
          <pose>-8.850 9.450 0.700 0 0 0</pose>
          <geometry><box><size>2.100 1.000 1.400</size></box></geometry>
        </collision>
        <visual name="a_bay0_level1_visual">
          <pose>-8.850 9.450 0.700 0 0 0</pose>
          <geometry><box><size>2.100 1.000 1.400</size></box></geometry>
          <material><ambient>0.72 0.56 0.34 1</ambient><diffuse>0.72 0.56 0.34 1</diffuse></material>
        </visual>
        <collision name="a_bay0_level2_collision">
          <pose>-8.850 9.450 2.100 0 0 0</pose>
          <geometry><box><size>2.100 1.000 1.200</size></box></geometry>
        </collision>
        <visual name="a_bay0_level2_visual">
